.Dd November 19, 2026
.Dt TACOLINUX 7
.Os TacoLinux
.Sh NAME
.Nm tacolinux
.Nd the read-the-manual Linux distribution
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a small, self-contained Linux distribution built from a minimal base
rootfs plus a closure of statically linked command-line tools.
It is installed by hand: partition a disk, copy the root filesystem
with
.Xr rsync 1 ,
and run
.Xr grub-install 8 .
There is no graphical installer and no hand-holding.
.Pp
The default desktop session is
.Nm dwm .
.Nm xfce
is installed alongside it for when a full desktop is wanted.
Both are selected at the
.Nm sddm
greeter.
.Sh LOGGING IN
The image ships two accounts with known defaults:
.Bl -tag -width "tacolinux" -compact
.It Li taco Li / Li taco
the normal user, a member of the
.Li wheel
group.
.It Li root Li / Li tacolinux
the superuser, for console and recovery use.
.El
.Pp
The repository does not contain password hashes.
Both accounts are locked in
.Pa /etc/shadow
and the image build hashes the plaintext defaults above at build time,
using SHA-512 so that both PAM and the bundled static tools can verify them.
Change them after the first login with
.Xr passwd 1 .
.Pp
The
.Li taco
and
.Li wheel
accounts have passwordless
.Xr sudo 8
.Pq Li NOPASSWD: ALL ,
so
.Dl sudo -i
yields a root shell without a prompt.
.Xr su 1
is a static BusyBox binary installed setuid root; it asks for the target
user's password.
.Sh BUNDLED TOOLS
Every program in
.Pa /usr/local/bin
is a fully static musl binary with no
.Dv PT_INTERP ,
so it runs on the base system, in a chroot, or in a future rootfs without
depending on the Nix store for a C library.
.Pp
The set includes editors
.Pq nano , mg ,
pagers and browsers
.Pq less , links ,
utilities
.Pq tree , jq , bc , zstd , lz4 , tmux , screen , strace , lsof , socat , wget ,
and a full process and network toolbox.
The sources are vendored under
.Pa /sources
and the build is reproducible from
.Pa /scripts/build-cli-tools.sh .
.Pp
.Nm hyfetch
prints system information with pride-flag colours.
Its TacoLinux wordmark is stored in
.Pa /etc/tacolinux/hyfetch.ascii
and uses colour markers that any flag can fill.
The first run opens the setup wizard and asks which flag you want; run
.Dl hyfetch -c
to pick another one later, or
.Dl hyfetch -p transgender
for a single run.
.Pp
The manual itself is served by
.Xr mandoc 1 ,
also static.
The
.Nm man
command is a symlink to
.Nm mandoc ,
and this page is the distribution manual.
.Sh BROWSING
.Nm links
works in two modes from the same binary:
.Bl -tag -width "links -g" -compact
.It Li links
the text-mode browser, usable on a console or in a terminal.
.It Li links Fl g
the graphical browser, drawn with Links' built-in fonts on an X display.
.El
.Sh INSTALLING
Read
.Pa README.md
in the repository, then, from a rescue environment:
.Bl -enum
.It
Partition the target disk and create a boot and a root filesystem.
.It
Mount the root filesystem and extract the rootfs with
.Xr rsync 1 .
.It
Install GRUB to the disk.
.It
Reboot, log in, and read this manual again.
.El
.Pp
Prebuilt images are published for downloads; the tag builds are compressed
with
.Xr xz 1
and accompanied by a
.Pa SHA256SUMS
file so they remain usable from slow or filtered networks.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width MANPAGER -compact
.It Ev MANPAGER
pager used by
.Nm man ;
defaults to
.Xr less 1 .
.It Ev PAGER
fallback pager when
.Ev MANPAGER
is unset.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/share/tacolinux" -compact
.It Pa /etc/sudoers
passwordless sudo rules.
.It Pa /etc/pam.d/
PAM service stacks, including
.Pa passwd ,
.Pa chpasswd ,
.Pa su
and
.Pa su-l .
.It Pa /etc/login.defs
sets
.Dv ENCRYPT_METHOD SHA512 .
.It Pa /usr/local/bin/
statically linked CLI tools and the
.Nm man
symlink.
.It Pa /usr/local/share/tacolinux/cli-tools.txt
list of shipped CLI binaries.
.It Pa /usr/share/man/man7/tacolinux.7
this manual page.
.It Pa /scripts/build-vm-image.sh
builds a bootable image and sets the default passwords.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr links 1 ,
.Xr mandoc 1 ,
.Xr passwd 1 ,
.Xr rsync 1 ,
.Xr su 1 ,
.Xr grub-install 8 ,
.Xr sudo 8
.Pp
The full manual lives in
.Pa README.md
at the repository root.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An TacoLinux contributors
.Sh BUGS
Report issues at the project forge.
If it segfaults, it was probably a dynamically linked binary.
